## Report structure

### Memory hygiene summary (forgetting — not learning)

- Contradictions found: {{ findings | selectattr("issue_type", "equalto", "contradiction") | list | length }}
- Contradictions resolved: <count of approved + executed contradiction proposals>
- Fragmented memories found: {{ findings | selectattr("issue_type", "equalto", "fragmentation") | list | length }}
- Fragmented memories resolved: <count>
- Miscalibrated confidence found: {{ findings | selectattr("issue_type", "equalto", "miscalibrated_confidence") | list | length }}
- Confidence recalibrated: <count>
- Source memories purged (post-reification): <count>
- Source memories condensed (post-reification): <count>

### Reification summary (learning — closes the learning loop)

- Reification candidates found: {{ findings | selectattr("issue_type", "equalto", "reification_candidate") | list | length }}
- Skills created: <count>
- Templates created: <count>
- Rules created: <count>

### Per-issue detail

For each finding, report:
- **Finding**: ID, issue type, entity, description.
- **Process**: hygiene | reification | post-reification hygiene.
- **Proposal**: strategy, action, reason.
- **User decision**: approved / modified / rejected.
- **Execution**: success / failure, outcome.
- **Reification** (if applicable): what skill/template/rule was created.

### Recommendations

- Follow-up therapy sessions (e.g., "run another session after the next consolidation cycle").
- Skill effectiveness review (e.g., "review the new skill's effectiveness after N invocations").
- Remaining reification candidates (e.g., "3 reification candidates were not addressed — consider a follow-up session").
- Memory database health (e.g., "memory database is now at N h_mems, down from M — within storage budget").

## Output format

Produce a markdown report with the sections above. Be honest — report failures, report when nothing was found, do not fabricate success.
